        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Low back pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Central and paraspinal lumbar ache with deep stiffness, ongoing for approximately 3 months and more noticeable over the last 4–6 weeks. Worse with standing and walking; better with sitting and stretching. Morning stiffness lasts approximately 10 minutes then eases. Baseline pain 3/10, flaring to 6/10. No clear injury; patient thinks a softer new mattress and long periods at the computer may contribute. No leg radiation, pins and needles, or weakness. Denies saddle numbness and bladder or bowel issues. No fevers, weight loss, night sweats, or waking from sleep with pain. Mobilising independently but cutting back longer walks."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
